~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Trains the final predictive model and tests variants on compounds the model never saw (15% of
  the data is set         aside before anything else happens, so the test is honest):
  Exp A - baseline: a stacking ensemble (several different algorithms whose predictions are
  combined by a final model).         Exp B - A plus feature selection: keeps only the fingerprint
  bits that actually help prediction (permutation         importance: a bit is useful if randomly
  scrambling it makes predictions worse). The importance is computed out-of-fold         inside
  the development set: each model is scored on molecules it was not fitted on, so a bit is kept
  only if it helps         predict unseen molecules, not if the trees merely memorised it.
  Exp C - B plus data augmentation: adds slightly noisy copies of the training molecules'
  potencies (Gaussian noise) to         see whether this makes the model more robust.         Exp
  Bleaky / Exp Cleaky - diagnostics only: the same as B and C, but the bits are selected by
  permuting on the TEST         set, as the original study did. The test molecules then influence
  the model, so these scores are optimistically         biased; comparing them with B and C
  measures how much of a reported gain can come from that leak. They never feed         the saved
  mask or models.
  Metrics: R2 (1 = perfect, 0 = no better than predicting the mean potency) and MAE (average error
  in pIC50 units;         0.5 means a typical error of ~3-fold in IC50). The 95% CI comes from
  bootstrap resampling of the test set: it shows how         much the score would move if a
  different sample of test molecules had been drawn. With so few test molecules the CI is
  wide, so small R2 differences between experiments are often not meaningful.
  Outputs used downstream: results/04_best_model.joblib (the un-augmented model used for the
  virtual screening in step 05)         and results/04_selected_features_mask.npy (which
  fingerprint bits are kept).
